  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.4. Strengthened social dialogue and labour relations laws, processes and institutions</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Mediation and Arbitration Organization (OMED) of Greece was restructured and strengthened through Article 98 of Law 4808 of June 2021 for better effectiveness by absorbing the mediation and conciliation competences previously held by the labour inspection services (SEPE) over individual labour disputes. Following consultations with the tripartite constituents, the ILO formulated policy recommendations in June 2020 to address some areas of possible changes in the Greek labour law framework that could modernise the national dispute settlement system. These policy recommendations were based on international labour standards; relevant comments by the ILO supervisory bodies; and comparative practices. They were also based on a comparative background report commissioned by the project, on &quot;Individual and collective labour dispute settlement systems&quot;. Finally, they took into account the conclusions of the ILO 2012 Labour Inspection Needs Assessment Report (Greece), and of the 2017 and the ILO Assessment of the Greek Labour Administration.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.4.1. Number of member States with newly developed or strengthened institutions, mechanisms or regulatory frameworks for social dialogue, labour relations or dispute prevention/resolution that address current and emerging challenges in the world of work</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
